## Failure

`tests/test_jetp_courbe_reference.py::test_chaine_portee_reproduit_la_reference`
fails at line 68 because `data/jetp/crs` is absent in a fresh 0876 worktree.
The test intentionally fails rather than skipping: it needs the archived
80 `*_micro.csv.gz` files to replay the pinned CRS calculation and compare
the output cell by cell with
`conception/jetp/papier-court-mesure/courbe-reference-decaissement-2026-09-08.csv`.
The test never reached the comparison, so the result establishes missing
test data, not a successful or failed numerical reproduction.

`make jetp-data` only checks out JETP documents and a VNM release
(`Makefile:234-237`); it does not fetch CRS. The dedicated
`jetp-crs-data` target at `Makefile:150-151` runs `dvc pull data/jetp/crs`.
This full-gate prerequisite was not run in the worktree. The four separate
country-scan failures in the same full suite are tracked in [[0940]].

## Work

- Verify that the pinned CRS DVC object is available from the configured
  remote and that `make jetp-crs-data` materializes exactly 80 archived
  `*_micro.csv.gz` inputs in a fresh worktree. If retrieval fails, capture
  the concrete remote/cache error and restore the missing pinned object.
- Make the full-gate setup state the CRS prerequisite before starting the
  14-minute suite, or materialize it as part of the documented full-gate
  workflow. Keep the test's fail-when-absent behavior.
- Rerun the named integration test and compare every output row with the
  versioned reference; retain the pinned 98.56% and 37.35% central figures.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make jetp-crs-data` succeeds in a fresh worktree and exactly 80
  `*_micro.csv.gz` files are present under `data/jetp/crs`.
- [ ] The named reference-chain integration test passes and its output is
  byte/cell equivalent to the versioned reference as asserted by the test.
- [ ] The full-gate workflow catches missing CRS inputs before the main test
  suite, with an actionable command; it never silently skips this test.
